## 1. What the app has today (the delta)

Roster (profile rows + day-grouped session rows, 25/page) · Thread (history, composer, SSE token
stream, working Stop) · Settings (base URL, key, extra profiles, model) · connectivity layer (ordered
route candidates by role+priority, Tailscale trigger module, honest failure banner) · PT-PT
throughout · **60 offline tests** + `mock/` gateway (a build loop that runs with no phone and no key).
Shipped today: `dist/personae-0.3.0.apk`, versionCode 3, same release key (upgrades in place over
0.1.0/0.2.0).

Everything below is what the plugin does and the app does **not**.

---

## 2. Parity matrix

### Bucket A — API supports it; mobile just needs to render/act

| Plugin feature | API |
|---|---|
| Profile → that profile's sessions, newest first | `GET /api/sessions` (`/p/<profile>/` prefix for extra profiles) |
| Open session, full history | `GET /api/sessions/{id}/messages` |
| Compose + streamed reply, **Stop** | `POST .../chat/stream` · `/chat` · `POST /v1/runs/{id}/stop` |
| New session with a profile | `POST /api/sessions` |
| Rename | `PATCH /api/sessions/{id}` `{title}` |
| Pin | `PATCH {pinned}` |
| Archive | `PATCH {archived}` |
| Hide (unfiled) | `PATCH {hidden}` |
| Delete | `DELETE /api/sessions/{id}` |
| Fork / branch | `POST /api/sessions/{id}/fork` |
| Parent↔child links, ↳ / ↩ markers | `parent_session_id`, `_lineage_root_id` |
| Mark read/unread (**write** side) | `PATCH {unread}` → `db.set_session_read` (both surfaces) |
| Row body: preview, age, message + tool counts, tokens, cost | `preview`, `last_active`, `message_count`, `tool_call_count`, cost fields |
| Per-session model lock | `POST /api/sessions/{id}/model` · `GET /api/model/options` |
| Bell / cron surface | `/api/jobs` (list/create/update/pause/resume/run/delete) · `/api/cron/fire` |

### Bucket B — REVISED: mostly served by the dashboard backend

| Plugin feature | Was | Now |
|---|---|---|
| **Profiles list** | no route → upstream | ✅ `GET /api/profiles` (`:9119`) — **consume it, don't build it** (D2) |
| **Cross-profile session rail** | hand-typed | ✅ `GET /api/profiles/sessions/sidebar` — the exact batched shape the pane needs |
| **Unread read-back** | write-only → upstream | ⚠️ write confirmed on both surfaces; read projection **unverified** — small fix either way (D3) |
| **Running / "blocked on you" dot** | RPC-only | ⚠️ hybrid: recently-active is free; true *pending-approval* needs a small route (D3) |
| **Avatars / thumbnails** | RPC-only | ❌ still RPC-only — expose `GET /api/profiles/{name}/avatar` (cheap) or ship initials (D2) |
| **Groups** (named sections inside a profile) | client store | **D1(a): phone-local** — 0 hits server-side for `messenger-session-groups`, so there is nothing to read. This is the only option, not a preference. |
| **Colours** (session / group, incl. "no fill") | client store | D1(a) phone-local |
| **Manual drag order + sort mode** | client store | D1(a) phone-local |
| **Apropos** (child session seeded with picked sessions' background) | client store + RPC | D1(a) + `POST /api/sessions/{id}/fork` for the child |
| **Bots identity parity** | app-local store + RPC | 🟡 partial: name/description/model are in `GET /api/profiles`; avatar is the gap |

### Bucket C — mobile builds it (no server question)

Expand/collapse a profile into its sessions · row geometry · long-press context menus (Open, Rename,
Colour, File into group, Sort, Copy id, Apropos, Delete) · multi-select + selection bar (bulk archive
/ delete / Apropos) · groups as drop targets · toolbar chrome (bell, **+**, folder+, search, filters)
· day grouping and pagination · status-dot aggregation (profile dot = aggregate of its sessions,
never its own) · PT-PT strings · theme.

**Search & filter is a trap:** the plugin's search is server-side over *profiles and sessions*. The
API only accepts `source`, exact `title`, `include_children`, `include_hidden` — **no text search, no
activity/kind/profile-set filters.** Filtering by profile is reachable via the `/p/<profile>/` prefix;
free-text search over session titles/previews would be a client-side filter over the fetched page.
State that honestly in the UI or add a server param.

---

## 3. Touch mapping — the plugin's affordances are mouse-shaped

| Plugin (mouse) | Phone |
|---|---|
| Right-click context menu | Long-press → action sheet |
| Hover states | None — affordance always visible |
| Drag row between groups / reorder groups | Long-press to lift, drop targets highlight |
| Ctrl/Cmd-click multi-select | "Selecionar" from the toolbar; tap rows to tick |
| Scroll + 25/page pagination | `FlatList` (virtualised) |

This mapping is in scope — without it, "all features" is not actually reachable on a phone.

---

## 4. Decisions

**Answered by you (2026-10-11):**

- **D1 = (a) phone-local** pane state (groups, colours, manual order, read markers → AsyncStorage).
  Confirmed as the *only* option: the server has no `messenger-*` state at all. Desktop groups will
  not appear on the phone until (b) — an opaque per-profile state blob both devices read.
- **D2 = use `/api/profiles`** — now free, because the dashboard already serves it.
- **D3 = close the gaps** — shrunk to two small items: unread read-back (verify then patch if
  needed) and the pending-approval state. Both are now *narrow* fixes, not new subsystems.

**New, from the transport question:**

- **D4 — transport: HYBRID (recommended).** `:9222` for talk (chat, SSE, runs, session actions —
  stable and streaming); `:9119` for the rail (profiles list, per-profile slices, totals, projects).
  Two adapters, one interface; if `:9119` is unreachable the rail falls back to hand-declared
  profiles + `GET /api/sessions`. Rejected: dashboard-only (loses streaming + the documented API),
  API-only (needs upstream work for data that already exists).
- **D5 — expose avatars?** Yes = one small dashboard route (`GET /api/profiles/{name}/avatar`).
  No = initials monogram. Recommend **yes**, it is mechanical and the pane is avatar-driven.

---

## 5. Phases (each ends in a verifiable artifact)

- **P0 — transport.** Dashboard adapter (`:9119`, bearer session token, `expo-secure-store`) behind
  the existing `src/api` interface; `:9222` stays. `verify:` mock serves both; rail renders from
  `/api/profiles` + `/sidebar`; 9119-down fallback proven.
- **P1** expand/collapse the rail into per-profile sessions. `verify:` mock-gateway test asserting
  rows come from the API and the profile dot is an aggregate of its sessions.
- **P2** session actions via long-press + the Bucket-A write calls. `verify:` each call asserted
  against the mock, incl. 409/404 paths.
- **P3** toolbar, search/scope filters with the honest client-side boundary.
- **P4** groups + colours + manual sort on local state (D1a).
- **P5** multi-select bulk actions.
- **P6** Apropos (scoped beta).
- **P7** iOS parity pass via EAS.

Each phase git-committed, `npm test` green, `tsc --noEmit` clean. Android first, then iOS.

---

## 6. Sequencing and gates

- ✅ **No collision.** Cody's remote-access run **finished** (48m 8s, pid gone, `logs/CODY-DONE.txt`).
  The wait-vs-worktree question is moot — the UI build runs in the **main tree**, where the Android
  toolchain is already warm (docker image, keystore, gradle cache). A worktree would force a fresh
  `npm install` + native prebuild for zero benefit.
- Two things the finished run changed in the live config, for the record: `https://…:10443` now
  proxies `:9222` (was the dashboard), and Funnel `:443 → :8100` is byte-identical. If D4 lands,
  the dashboard needs its own route — add `:10444 → :9119` rather than repointing `:10443`.
- You asked for a **frontier model on planning/gates**. This document *is* the gate artifact — it
  can go to Step5/Opus/Fable for review before Cody builds; Cody builds on deepseek-flash.
- Android first (the v0.1.0 freeze skips to the new UI), then iOS via EAS.
